# =============================================================
# WP taxonomy / author archives served UNDER /blog/ (the /category/*,
# /author/*, /tag/* rules above only catch the bare-root form; Yoast's
# live permalinks are /blog/category/... and /blog/author/...).
# =============================================================
/blog/category/*   /blog   301
/blog/category     /blog   301
/blog/author/*     /blog   301
/blog/author       /blog   301
/blog/tag/*        /blog   301

# =============================================================
# WP post permalinks (current Yoast shape): /blog/{slug}/ -> pretty URL.
# Every live post sits at /blog/{slug}/; without this rule those URLs
# 404 on beta after cutover. Single-segment only, so it never shadows
# the two-segment /blog/posts/* rewrite below.
# =============================================================
/blog/:slug/   /blog/posts/:slug   301
/blog/:slug    /blog/posts/:slug   301

# =============================================================
# Pretty blog URLs: /blog/posts/{slug} serves /blog/post.html while
# keeping the slug in the URL bar.
#
# IMPORTANT: destination is `/blog/post` (no .html). CF Pages auto-
# strips `.html` from any URL it serves directly — if we used
# `/blog/post.html` here, the auto-strip would turn this rewrite into
# a 308 redirect to `/blog/post`, dropping the slug. The extensionless
# form makes CF Pages internally resolve `/blog/post` to `/blog/post.html`
# without changing the URL.
# =============================================================
/blog/posts/*   /blog/post   200
/blog/posts/*/  /blog/post   200
